FIX FE NAV-TABLE SCALING (780): arrow navigation reached wrong menu screens

The four front-end menu-navigation tables (DAT_004698a4/a5/a6/a7 = left/up/
right/down neighbor of each screen, 4-byte stride) are int-typed symbols, so
Ghidra's (&DAT_004698a4)[iVar3] with iVar3=screen*4 scaled the byte index x4
(reading at screen*16). asm 0x45039b etc.: lea (,%ebx,4),%edi; mov
0x4698a4(%edi),%al = a BYTE at screen*4. Effect: from screen 1 (Select Car) a
RIGHT read offset 16 (screen 4's data) instead of 4 -> jumped to the wrong
screen (Information instead of Select Track), so the arrow route to the
track-select screen was unreachable. Cast the table base to (unsigned char*).
Pointer-scaling class (DAT_00466a20/a96 table cases).

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -40621,7 +40621,7 @@
       if ((_DAT_0075444a & 0x80) == 0) break;
       FUN_00451c40();
       Play_Click_FX();
-      uVar4 = (uint)(byte)(&DAT_004698a4)[iVar3];
+      uVar4 = (uint)((unsigned char*)&DAT_004698a4)[iVar3];
       if ((uVar4 == 2) && ((race_type == 4 || (race_type == 3)))) {
         uVar4 = 1;
       }
@@ -40700,7 +40700,7 @@
